sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Product X payment-status method switch
  accDescr: The initial submit-and-poll method times out. The event does not prove payment failure. The governor verifies that the goal and no-duplicate-charge invariant remain valid, authorizes a read-only reconciliation method, and records the method change without changing the goal. An authoritative result then permits satisfaction or continued suspension.
  participant U as User / principal
  participant I as Intention registry
  participant M1 as Submit and poll
  participant G as Method governor
  participant M2 as Read-only reconciliation
  participant P as Payment provider
  U->>I: Authorize status goal and no-duplicate invariant
  I->>M1: Execute method version 1 with idempotency key
  M1->>P: Submit original attempt
  P--xM1: Response timeout; status unknown
  M1->>G: Timeout event bound to goal and method version
  G->>I: Load current intention and verify version
  G->>G: Diagnose: goal remains valid; write retry unsafe
  G->>I: Commit method switch; preserve goal version
  I->>M2: Dispatch read-only reconciliation
  M2->>P: Query original attempt status
  P-->>M2: Authoritative status and attempt identifier
  M2->>I: Return evidence with provenance
  I->>G: Evaluate goal verification condition
  G->>I: Mark satisfied only when verified
